      "text": "To determine how many students did not receive an A in either math or history, we can use the principle of inclusion and exclusion. Let's denote the following:\n\n- \\( |H| \\) as the number of students who received an A in history.\n- \\( |M| \\) as the number of students who received an A in math.\n- \\( |H \\cap M| \\) as the number of students who received an A in both history and math.\n- \\( |H \\cup M| \\) as the number of students who received an A in either history or math or both.\n\nFrom the problem, we know:\n- \\( |H| = 7 \\)\n- \\( |M| = 13 \\)\n- \\( |H \\cap M| = 4 \\)\n\nAccording to the principle of inclusion and exclusion, the number of students who received an A in either history or math or both is given by:\n\\[ |H \\cup M| = |H| + |M| - |H \\cap M| \\]\nSubstituting the given values, we get:\n\\[ |H \\cup M| = 7 + 13 - 4 = 16 \\]\n\nThis means that 16 students received an A in either history or math or both. Since there are 30 students in total, the number of students who did not receive an A in either course is:\n\\[ 30 - |H \\cup M| = 30 - 16 = 14 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of students who did not receive an A in any of these two courses is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).",
